{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_10-13-13-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nR=\\\"b487504d6cf743fc8e70b4a75f79f0db\\\"\nupd={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Interpretation of the growth-repair receipt \\\"+R+\\\" (completed, exit_code 0) for the growth investigation, pursuing the concrete consequence the earlier interpretation left open: whether the cluster made leaderless by the documented growth step can be repaired through the same API. Parsed events: indices 28, 29 and 30 are the absent-server case (bounded write attempt, the two repair attempts plus the three-second unrepaired window, and recovery after the named server starts) and 33, 34 and 35 are the matching control. The predicate evaluated is whether the API that accepted the growth step can undo it while the named server is absent; it is contradicted, and the earlier finding keeps its scope while gaining this impact boundary. A fact records the consequence.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"b2266ae85cad4e4db077a5615b2b892c-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"8a50ad8127a545fc99e76be7f580e809-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"addvoter-doc-staging-promise\\\",\\\"bootstrapcluster-growth-guidance\\\",\\\"appendconfiguration-installs-latest\\\",\\\"commitment-recalculate-quorum\\\",\\\"checkleaderlease-latest-quorum\\\",\\\"quorumsize-latest\\\",\\\"requestconfigchange-timeout-scope\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{R:[29,30,28,34,35,33]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"666afbbf5c5b4554bbfdd6bc26504c5e-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The AddVoter step with an absent server commits and then leaves the only node a leaderless Candidate that refuses writes until the named server appears.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"b2266ae85cad4e4db077a5615b2b892c-knowledge-2\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"Configuration-change timeouts bound only the enqueue, so the caller gets no signal from the timeout about the stuck state.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Absent-server case (index 29): with the cluster still leaderless, RemoveServer for the absent server returns 'node is not the leader' and AddNonvoter for the same server returns the same error, so neither of the two natural ways to undo the growth step is accepted; over the following three seconds every sample shows the node as a Candidate at term 2 with commit index 3, unchanged from before the attempts, so nothing in the API moved it back. Index 28 is the bounded client write in the same state, also refused with 'node is not the leader', and index 30 shows the only observed repair: once the named server is started at its announced address the original node becomes Leader at term 3 and its commit index advances to 4, with the named node following as a Follower. Control (indices 33, 34, 35): with the named server running from the start, the same client write succeeds (no error, commit 4) and both repair calls return no error (RemoveServer and AddNonvoter both accepted, because a leader exists to serve them), the node staying Leader with commit 6 over the same three-second window. Reading the two together: the refusals are not a property of the API but of the leaderless state the documented growth step creates, and the state is only repairable by the event the caller controls (starting the named server) or by an offline recovery route that this experiment did not execute. Predicate evaluated: following the documented growth sequence, with the next server not yet running, must not leave the cluster in a state that the API cannot repair. It is contradicted: at least 4.5 seconds of observed leaderlessness (1500 ms window plus the 3000 ms repair window) with every in-process repair attempt refused, while the same API calls succeed in the control. Scope: protocol version 3, a single-voter configuration grown by one voter, no faults, one process, in-memory transport.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"The same calls succeed when a leader exists (control, index 34), so the refusals are a consequence of the leaderless state rather than a difference in the API's behaviour between the two cases.\\\",\n   \\\"The state is repairable without the API: starting the named server restores leadership and progress within the same execution (index 30), which is the step the documented sequence implies but documents as automatic.\\\",\n   \\\"The library also offers an offline recovery route (RecoverCluster) for a cluster that has lost quorum, and this experiment did not execute it, so the claim is about in-process API repair, not about every possible repair.\\\",\n   \\\"The observations cover 4.5 seconds of leaderlessness with 25 ms and 50 ms sampling; a later self-repair beyond that window is not claimed, and the source shows no such path while the server is absent.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"One retained execution; the two repair attempts are bounded by a 1200 ms timer each, so a repair that would only complete later is not covered.\\\",\n   \\\"Only the single-voter growth step is exercised; configurations whose new quorum can be met by the survivors are unaffected and were not measured here.\\\",\n   \\\"The offline recovery route and any out-of-process intervention were not executed.\\\",\n   \\\"In-memory transport, one process, default protocol version, and the control case runs on a separate cluster instance built in the same execution.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"This receipt comes from the same harness lineage and staging as the earlier growth receipt, with two bounded repair attempts and a three-second unrepaired window added; its absent-server case re-witnesses the deposition and recovery on a fresh process, and its control is the same staging with the named server running from the start.\\\",\n  \\\"report_title\\\":\\\"文档推荐的扩展步骤造成的无领导者状态无法用同一 API 修复：RemoveServer 与 AddNonvoter 均被拒绝\\\",\n  \\\"report_answer\\\":\\\"针对第三条发现的直接后果，本次保留执行 \\\"+R+\\\" 确认：按库自身文档的顺序（先启动单节点、再 AddVoter 一台尚未运行的服务器）之后，集群处于无领导者状态，此时用同一 API 尝试撤销该步骤（RemoveServer 指名服务器、AddNonvoter 指名服务器）都会得到 'node is not the leader'，随后 3 秒内该节点始终保持 Candidate、term 恒为 2、commit 恒为 3，没有任何进展；客户端写入同样被拒。对照（同一调用，但命名服务器一开始就在运行）中，同样两个 API 调用都成功返回（因为有领导者可服务），节点保持 Leader、commit 持续推进到 6。唯一被观察到的修复是在命名地址上启动那台服务器：原节点随即在 term 3 重新当选并恢复提交。结论：该状态在进程内无法用 API 自修复（离线 RecoverCluster 路径本次未执行），符合此前记录的『AddVoter future 返回成功但集群不可用』这一缺陷；缺陷主张维持，影响边界新增『至少 4.5 秒无领导者且进程内无可用的撤销手段』。\\\"\n }],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\n  \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@absent-voter-step-unrepairable-in-process\\\",\n  \\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"After the documented growth step has made a single-voter cluster leaderless because the newly named server is absent, the same API cannot undo it: RemoveServer and AddNonvoter for that server both return ErrNotLeader, a client write is refused with the same error, and the node remains a Candidate with an unchanged term and a pinned commit index for the whole observed window; the only observed repair is starting the named server, after which the original node wins an election and progress resumes.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Protocol version 3, one-voter configuration grown by one voter with the new server not running, no faults, in-memory transport; 1500 ms of sampling after the growth call plus two bounded (1200 ms) repair attempts and a further three seconds of sampling. The control with the named server running beforehand accepts both repair calls and keeps serving.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"addvoter-doc-staging-promise\\\",\\\"bootstrapcluster-growth-guidance\\\",\\\"checkleaderlease-latest-quorum\\\",\\\"quorumsize-latest\\\",\\\"requestconfigchange-timeout-scope\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{R:[29,30,28,34,35]}\n }]\n}\nopen('update.json','w').write(json.dumps(upd,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nprint('ok', json.load(open('update.json'))['interpretations'][0]['conclusion'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
